      "id": "m1",
      "title": "Implement CSV parsing and row-to-object mapping",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "## Objective\nImplement parseCsv(text) and toObjects(rows) in src/csv.js.\n\n## Requirements\n- parseCsv returns an array of rows; each row is an array of string fields.\n- Fields are separated by commas.\n- A field wrapped in double quotes may contain commas and line breaks; a doubled quote inside it means one double quote character.\n- Lines end with LF or CRLF. A final line break does not add an empty row. Empty text returns [].\n- toObjects treats the first parsed row as the header and returns one object per remaining row, keyed by header; a short row gets empty strings for missing columns.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- c1: comma-separated fields, c2: quoted fields with commas/newlines and doubled-quote escape, c3: LF/CRLF and trailing-newline/empty-text behavior, c4: header mapping with padding.\n- npm test passes with tests covering each criterion, including edge cases named above.",
      "preview": null,
      "dispatch": null,
